If a hydrogen fuel cell car was for sale today,

106
00:08:37,781 --> 00:08:42,020
it'd probably cost hundreds of thousands of dollars.

107
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:43,780
Time and technological breakthroughs

108
00:08:43,781 --> 00:08:45,860
will bring prices down.

109
00:08:45,861 --> 00:08:48,060
But it could take 15 to 30 years

110
00:08:48,061 --> 00:08:50,520
before practical and affordable hydrogen fuel cell

111
00:08:50,521 --> 00:08:52,160
vehicles are available to the public.

112
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:57,480
Hopefully, the promise of a hydrogen economy

113
00:08:57,481 --> 00:08:59,680
is worth the wait.

114
00:08:59,681 --> 00:09:04,380
The idea of being able to have pollution-free driving

115
00:09:04,381 --> 00:09:09,620
And in fact, having a diverse source of hydrogen, I think, is pretty damn exciting.

116
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,300
And I think people would love that.

117
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:16,240
Now, unfortunately, it doesn't help you with the congestion.

