422
00:29:40,121 --> 00:29:43,760
and a direct connection between his brain and a computer.

423
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:47,560
Matthew is a quadriplegic,

424
00:29:47,561 --> 00:29:49,480
paralyzed from the neck down.

425
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:56,540
In 2004, he became the first recipient of a BMI implant called BrainGate.

426
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:05,240
BrainGate actually taps into the real signals that orchestrate hand motions.

427
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:13,780
The idea is to tap into the part of the brain that gives the commands to move your hand.

428
00:30:13,781 --> 00:30:18,780
This reddish strip right here is called the motor cortex.

429
00:30:18,781 --> 00:30:21,780
This is the part of the cerebral cortex that controls movement,

430
00:30:21,781 --> 00:30:26,780
and it's separated into subdivisions so that control of your leg is from up here,

431
00:30:26,781 --> 00:30:29,780
control of the arm is down here, and control of the face is down here.

432
00:30:29,781 --> 00:30:33,780
So if we're interested in signals for controlling the arm, we know right where to go.

433
00:30:35,780 --> 00:30:37,780
Equipped with a road map of Matthew's brain,

434
00:30:37,781 --> 00:30:42,780
a neurosurgeon cut a hole in his skull and implanted a tiny sensor

435
00:30:42,781 --> 00:30:44,760
with 100 hair-thin electrodes.

436
00:30:47,540 --> 00:30:50,600
The electrodes penetrated into the surface of his brain.

437
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:53,960
The sensor was attached to a connector,

438
00:30:54,500 --> 00:30:56,240
which was fastened to the patient's skull.

439
00:30:58,360 --> 00:30:59,960
One month after the surgery,

440
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:02,040
the team held their collective breath

441
00:31:02,041 --> 00:31:05,580
as Matthew was plugged in for the first time.

442
00:31:07,340 --> 00:31:09,640
After being cut off for three years,

443
00:31:10,100 --> 00:31:11,660
